				Input10 = InstanceInput {
					SourceOp = "bol_add",
					Source = "EffectMask",
				},
				Comments = Input {
					Value = "Grain Macro to replace Fusion's own grain tool, in many cases the original tool cannot generate small enough grain. This Macro adds the grain in a gamma corrected space so the grain should work more natural in the highlights and shadows.\n\nSize: Sets the size of the grain, smaller values mean bigger grain.\n\nPower: The amplitude of the grain. The main Power slider value is added to the individual channels.\n\nDisplacemant: Used to displace the center of amplitude of the grain. In experience we found that sometimes the grain has a littel overall color displacement.\n\nSoftness: Blurs the channel.\n\nHighlight/Shadow Gain: Usefull in correcting the way the grain reacts in the highlights and the shadows. Possibility to unlock the channels.\nSaturation: If you want to desaturate the grain for monochrome use.\n\n\n\nIn 5.3 build 55 there is a bug with the expression to set the size of the grain. I will also put up a version where you can manully adjust the resolution. In Build 66 the bug is fixed. I don't know about older versions probably also have the bug.\n\nTodo: Add another layer of darker more random grain, this sometimes is seen in the grain. \n\nKasper Oerlemans\nFilmmore Amsterdam\nNovember 2008",
				},
			},
